  "provenance": "All 55 prior quantitative artifacts/rows/defaults remain byte-identical. CVX-054 adds five pinned new shared-primitives supplied-contract tests/fixture/standalone example, with exact dates, annualized decimal rates, absolute cash units, primary-source identities and analytic bounds (1e-24 absolute/zero relative; published NY Fed index precision eight decimals). Engineering-derived evidence, not admitted market packs or independent quantitative approval. No older tolerance or kernel test is refreshed. CVX-056 appends five new supplied-contract/analytic curve and economic term conservation artifacts. All 60 prior artifact rows/bytes and solver defaults are preserved. Native f64 tolerance 1e-11 absolute plus 1e-11 relative; exact dates/units/Decimal economics unchanged. No independent quantitative approval or library/model certificate is claimed. CVX-060 appends four new analytic numerical/transform test, fixture and standalone consumer artifacts. All 65 earlier rows/bytes/defaults remain unchanged. Supplied negative-rate DF reference uses independent 50-digit Python Decimal exp. Declared absolute1e-11 plus relative1e-11 bounds, tighter explicit short-period checks, native objective/quote thresholds and 512 seeded generated cases do not claim independent quantitative approval or a market/library certificate. CVX-017 appends five engineering candidate artifacts: 13 supplied dated bond cases with independent Decimal(50) calculation, actual native/C ABI and admitted REST parity, explicit role/failure controls and standalone facade. All 69 earlier rows/bytes/defaults and retained QuantLib reference values/tolerances remain unchanged. New absolute price/risk 1e-9 plus relative1e-11 bounds and accrued/yield1e-10 checks are engineering declarations, not independent quantitative approval. Correcting coupon/payment discount steps resolves all 105 historical comparison misses on the same 392 references; original failing captures remain historical evidence. Market/model and full-surface certificates remain pending. CVX-055 appends four supplied bond engineering artifacts: 10 independently declared Decimal(50) cash/PV cases, native eligible-history/overnight/exercise tests, analytic valuation tests and a real standalone facade. All 74 earlier rows, bytes, expected values, tolerances and solver defaults remain unchanged. New absolute cash1e-22 and price1e-9 plus relative1e-11 bounds, and 128 seeded exact step/principal cases, are engineering declarations rather than independent quantitative approval. Unsupported market/model/host combinations fail explicitly; full certificates remain pending. CVX-059 appends five engineering artifacts for 12 independent math.erfc European ZCB options, three actual-dated swaption quotations, notice exchange option, joint term-FRN margin option, analytic optional risk at explicit 50/100/200bp bumps, positive/failure tests and standalone facade. New scoped option premium2e-7, lattice price0.004+1e-8 relative, sigma2e-7, duration0.005/convexity0.5/PV01-per100 5e-5 declarations include existing CDF approximation and kinked-grid limits. Undersampled 1bp risk fails explicitly. Preserve every earlier 78 row/byte/expectation/tolerance/default. These independent engineering calculations do not assert independent human quantitative approval, admitted market packs or complete model/host/LB certificates.",
